  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0019 database is designed to manage various aspects of user accounts, projects, and API-related data. At its core, it contains a table called accounts_profile, which stores information about user accounts, including their next report date, reports allowed, and various limits such as ping log, check, and SMS limits. Each account is associated with a user from the auth_user table, which stores user credentials, login history, and other details. The accounts_project table links projects to their owners, who are also users from the auth_user table. The accounts_member table connects users to projects they are a part of. The api_channel table stores information about API channels, including their code, kind, and last error, and is linked to projects through the accounts_project table. The api_check table contains details about API checks, such as their code, status, and schedule, and is associated with projects through the accounts_project table. The api_flip table tracks changes in the status of API checks, while the api_notification table stores notifications sent to API channels. The api_ping table logs API pings, including their method, scheme, and body, and is linked to API checks. The api_tokenbucket table manages tokens, including their value, tokens available, and last update. The payments_subscription table stores information about user subscriptions, including their customer ID, payment method, and plan details, and is linked to users through the auth_user table.",
  "gold_question": "Cron Monitoring Tool \n\n 1) Background / Context\nThe project involves developing a cron monitoring tool as a Django application. This tool is designed to provide alerts when nightly backups, weekly reports, cron jobs, or scheduled tasks fail to execute on time. It aims to help users ensure the reliability of their scheduled tasks by notifying them of any discrepancies.\n\n 2) Objectives\nThe primary objective is to offer a simple and effective monitoring solution for cron jobs and scheduled tasks. The application should enable users to configure checks and receive timely notifications if tasks do not run according to schedule.\n\n 3) Stakeholders & Users\n- System Administrators: Responsible for configuring checks and monitoring scheduled tasks.\n- Developers: May use the tool for monitoring development and deployment tasks.\n- Teams: Benefit from shared alerts and monitoring insights.\n- Owners: Manage and access reports and team configurations.\n\n 4) Functional Descriptions\n- Alerts and Notifications: Sends alerts when scheduled tasks are overdue.\n- Dashboard: Provides a live-updating interface listing checks for each task.\n- Configuration: Allows naming and tagging checks, and setting Period and Grace Time.\n- Cron Expressions: Supports defining expected ping dates and times using cron expressions.\n- Event Logging: Maintains logs of received pings and sent notifications.\n- Status Badges: Offers public badges reflecting the status of tasks.\n\n Database Integration\n- Profile Management: Stores user profiles, report limits, and notification settings.\n- Project Management: Manages projects, their API keys, and related checks.\n- Channel Management: Handles notification channels and their configurations.\n- Check Management: Stores and manages the status and configuration of checks.\n- Notification & Ping Logging: Logs notifications and pings for reporting and troubleshooting.\n\n 5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n- Scalability: Supports a large number of concurrent checks and notifications.\n- Security: Ensures secure handling of API keys and notification channels.\n- Usability: Provides a user-friendly interface and simple configuration process.\n- Performance: Ensures real-time updates with minimal latency in alerting users.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0019.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0019\nCREATE TABLE `auth_user` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_login` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `accounts_profile` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `next_report_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reports_allowed` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ping_log_limit` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `check_limit` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sms_limit` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_profile_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `auth_user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `accounts_project` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `owner_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_project_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`owner_id`) REFERENCES `auth_user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `accounts_member` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_member_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `auth_user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `accounts_member_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_project` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `api_channel` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `code` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `kind` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `last_error` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `api_channel_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_project` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `api_check` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `code` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `schedule` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `api_check_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `accounts_project` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `api_flip` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `check_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `timestamp` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `api_flip_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`check_id`) REFERENCES `api_check` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `api_notification` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `channel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `message` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `sent_at` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `api_notification_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`channel_id`) REFERENCES `api_channel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `api_ping` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `check_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `method` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `scheme` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `body` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `api_ping_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`check_id`) REFERENCES `api_check` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `api_tokenbucket` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `value` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `tokens_available` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `last_update` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `payments_subscription` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_id` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `payment_method` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `plan_details` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `payments_subscription_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `auth_user` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
